# Docker Compose deployment
#
# Placeholder values used by `docker compose config` on a laptop. The real file
# lives on the VPS and is never committed (see docs/deployment.md).
#
# API_DOMAIN is both the public API hostname and the mail server's own name (FQDN).
# There is deliberately only one hostname: Caddy obtains one certificate for it, and the
# mail server presents that same certificate. The mail domain is derived from it by
# dropping the first label (api.example.invalid -> example.invalid), so the DNS records
# for SPF, DKIM, and DMARC belong to that derived domain.
#
# FRONTEND_ORIGIN is the exact origin the browser frontend is served from, and
# MAIL_ABSENDER is the envelope sender. MAIL_ABSENDER need not be a mailbox on the mail
# server: spoof protection is off by default there, so the submission account may send as
# any address in the domain.
API_DOMAIN=api.example.invalid
FRONTEND_ORIGIN=https://example.invalid
MAIL_ABSENDER=noreply@example.invalid
SUPERUSER_EMAIL=

# Written by `deploy:vps` on every start: the image it started last and the directory
# holding `data/` and `secrets/`. It also links the checkout's `.env` to this file, so a
# plain `docker compose up -d` in the checkout restarts the deployed stack. Compose
# refuses to render without either. On a laptop, use `compose.build.yaml` for the image
# and set the host root to `.` with a `secrets/mail.env` in the checkout.
# LOGANDAIM_IMAGE=ghcr.io/timerertim/logandaim-server:sha-<commit>
# LOGANDAIM_HOST_ROOT=/opt/logandaim
